      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(mcp): MCP disabled: true silently ignored — gateway spawns server processes anyway",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #103954 — When an MCP server entry in `openclaw.json` has `disabled: true` set, the gateway still spawns server processes for that entry. The `disabled` flag is silently ignored.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`McpServerConfig` has an `enabled?: boolean` field with doc \"Set false to keep the saved definition while excluding it from runtime/probe sessions\" — but it was **never checked** anywhere in the codebase. The field existed on the type but had no effect.\n\nAdditionally, users naturally reach for `disabled: true` (the convention used in the issue report) rather than the canonical `enabled: false`.\n\nThis fix normalizes `disabled` to `enabled` in **both** normalization paths:\n\n1. **`canonicalizeConfiguredMcpServer`** — called when writing config via `openclaw mcp set` commands. Normalizes `disabled` → `enabled` and strips `disabled` from the stored config.\n2. **`normalizeConfiguredMcpServers`** — called at runtime when loading config. Same normalization for entries read from disk.\n\nWhen both `enabled` and `disabled` are present, `enabled` wins (canonical field takes priority). When only `disabled` is set, it maps to the inverse of `enabled`.\n\nAll **four** existing `enabled === false` guard points automatically catch the normalized value:\n1. `bundle-mcp-config.ts` — tombstone + enable filter for config merge\n2. `bundle-mcp-codex.ts` — Codex app-server config generation\n3. `tool-policy-declared-context.ts` — tool policy context\n4. User config vs bundle default merging\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Setting `disabled: true` on an MCP server entry now prevents the gateway from spawning it\n- The canonical `enabled: false` continues to work as before (unchanged behavior)\n- `openclaw mcp set` commands normalize `disabled` out of the stored config\n- If both `enabled: true` and `disabled: true` are somehow set, `enabled` wins\n- No database or schema migration needed\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `oxlint`: 0 warnings / 0 errors\n- `tsgo:prod`: passes (TypeScript strict mode)\n- 16 tests pass across 3 test files:\n  - `mcp-config.test.ts` (8 tests)\n  - `bundle-mcp-config.test.ts` (4 tests)\n  - `tool-policy-declared-context.test.ts` (4 tests)\n\n```bash\n$ pnpm exec oxlint src/config/mcp-config-normalize.ts\nFound 0 warnings and 0 errors.\n\n$ pnpm tsgo:prod\n[no errors]\n\n$ pnpm vitest run src/config/mcp-config.test.ts src/agents/bundle-mcp-config.test.ts src/agents/tool-policy-declared-context.test.ts\nTest Files 3 passed\nTests 16 passed\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/mcp-disabled-flag",
